# A stable name for the DUT's console.
#
# Cheap USB/TTL adapters carry no serial number, so there is nothing unique
# about the device to match on. What is stable is the physical USB port: as
# long as the cable goes back into the same socket, KERNELS is the same
# string. That makes the name a property of where you plugged it rather than
# of the order things enumerated.
#
# KERNELS must be adapted to the port actually used. Find it with:
#
#   udevadm info -a -n /dev/ttyUSB0 | grep -m3 -E 'KERNELS|idVendor|idProduct'
#
# The value below is a placeholder and will not match anything until it is
# edited. That is deliberate: a rule that matched every tty would name the
# wrong device the first time a second adapter appeared.
#
# Everything downstream uses /dev/tty-dut3 and never ttyUSB0. Allocation
# order is not a promise, and ser2net holding the wrong device node is a
# lab that silently tests nothing.
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", KERNELS=="1-1.3", SYMLINK+="tty-dut3", GROUP="dialout", MODE="0660"
